[2026-10-02 17:50:54 EDT]   [Review] What worked: The team-preview read was sound: Kingambit is the correct anti-Psychic-Terrain piece (immune to Expanding Force, Psychic-resistant) and it did kill Indeedee-F, removing Follow Me/Psychic Terrain. Whimsicott got Tailwind up turn 1. Garchomp's Earthquake correctly spread-KO'd the grounded Psychic-Seed Sneasler on the last turn.
[2026-10-02 17:50:54 EDT]   [Review] What failed: 1) We never attacked Mega Gardevoir, their single win condition. Turn 1 and Turn 2 both actions went into Indeedee behind Follow Me — Follow Me redirected Kingambit's Iron Head on T2, so the 'Iron Head OHKOs Mega Gardevoir' plan was impossible by construction and the pilot's own calc line was a lie: with Follow Me up, any single-target move is forced into Indeedee. 2) T2 Whimsicott Protect at 14% was a wasted action in a game where Hyper Voice (spread) hits through Protect's partner slot anyway and Kingambit was dying — we should have Moonblasted Gardevoir or Encored it into Hyper Voice. 3) Three turns of double-action spent on a Follow Me support while the Mega killed Kingambit through chip. 4) Bringing Drogon into a board with Mega Gardevoir (Expanding Force 56-104%) + Sneasler (Dire Claw) was a death sentence; Drogon was slept and KO'd without ever acting. 5) The real Hyper Voice damage source was spread chip onto Kingambit (55% T1) which no one accounted for — Kingambit died to residual spread damage, not a direct attack.
[2026-10-02 17:50:54 EDT] [Team Inspiration] Recorded suggestion inspired by opponent build: "Copy their redirection+Mega funnel: pair a single unstoppable spread Mega with a Follow Me body. For us, that means always pairing Mega Charizard-Y's Heat Wave with Whimsicott and bringing Garchomp as the Follow-Me-proof spread option — and consider giving Whimsicott Helping Hand over Moonblast so the Mega's spread move is the win condition instead of chip damage." (Reason: Indeedee's Follow Me bought Mega Gardevoir two completely free turns; the only reason that worked is that our entire board was single-target. Spread offense plus redirection is the strongest structure in this meta.)
