[2026-10-02 18:09:50 EDT]   [Review] What worked: Turn 1 Tailwind went up immediately and Drogon Mega-evolved to flip rain into sun. Turn 2 focus-fire (Moonblast chip + Weather Ball) cleanly removed Mega Gengar, the Shadow Tag/Perish Song trapper, before it could trap anything — that was the correct macro target. Turn 4 Dragon Claw finished Pelipper (support engine) rather than overkilling.
[2026-10-02 18:09:50 EDT]   [Review] What failed: 1) Turn 1 Drogon attacked into a 100% certain Fake Out from Infernape and lost its action anyway (predictable Fake Out from a fresh Infernape lead — Protect or a non-committal move was better, or at minimum the Mega should not have been the Fake Out target of choice). 2) Turn 3 was the game-losing turn: both our mons were flagged with OHKO threats, Whimsicott was at 1 HP, and we attacked with both. Drogon (our Mega and only win condition) died to Electro Shot. The correct play was Drogon Protect (Archaludon had just switched in; Electro Shot charges in rain and is instant) while Whimsicott chips. 3) We let Archaludon charge Electro Shot unopposed and gain +1 SpA, then Stamina +1 Def — the opponent achieved speed (Pelipper could have had Tailwind) AND power with zero resistance. 4) Kingambit chipped Archaludon for 51% instead of us focus-firing it with both actions on T4; Archaludon then 1-shot Kingambit and Garchomp. 5) Garchomp was Choice-locked into Dragon Claw against a Steel/Dragon wall with +1 Def and had no out.
[2026-10-02 18:09:50 EDT] [Team Inspiration] Recorded suggestion inspired by opponent build: "Copy their 'disruption lead into charging nuke' structure: Gengar+Infernape existed purely to burn our turn-1 and turn-5 actions (Fake Out, Sludge Bomb) while Archaludon came in free and charged Electro Shot in Pelipper's rain. For us: keep Milotic as the mandatory 4th vs any rain sheet (max HP / max SpD, Leftovers) so Electro Shot and Aura Sphere are 3HKOs rather than OHKOs, and give Drogon a bulk-leaning spread (enough HP to survive one unboosted Electro Shot in rain) so it is not deleted before sun pays off." (Reason: Every one of our Pokemon was OHKO'd or near-OHKO'd by a single Archaludon; we had no body that could take two hits from it, so it never had to respect our offense.)
