[2026-10-02 19:14:55 EDT]   [Review] What worked: Won 2-0 in Pokémon count vs swampflower1's rain/TR-flavoured team. Turn 1 Kingambit lead was correct: it is immune to Expanding Force/Psychic and Kowtow Cleave ignores Protect, and Charizard's Drought immediately overwrote the incoming rain and let Heat Wave chip Sceptile + burn Pelipper. Recognising Dragapult's Phantom Force semi-invulnerable turn (T4) and redirecting both actions onto Sceptile was a clean, textbook action-economy save and got the KO. T3 switching Kingambit out at 26% instead of letting it eat Earth Power preserved our endgame win condition — Kingambit later KO'd Inteleon and Dragapult and closed the game 1v1. Sucker Punch on the final turn vs an attacking Dragapult was legal (no Psychic Terrain, no Armor Tail) and converted.
[2026-10-02 19:14:56 EDT]   [Review] What failed: 1) Drogon lost at T4: we committed both of our actions to Sceptile while Drogon was at 16% HP after Sceptile Dragon Pulse was clearly in range; the low-HP slot should have Protected (our own rule: slot at/below 25% HP with threats on board only Protects or switches). 2) Two misses (Weather Ball T3, Moonblast T5) cost tempo — both were sub-100% accuracy clicks while we were ahead; the safe-play accuracy bias exists in code but did not stop a 100%-accurate Moonblast miss (Moonblast is 100, so that was pure luck) while Weather Ball missing was the real damage. Actually Weather Ball is 100% too — the misses came from Phantom Force/evasion timing, not accuracy choices. 3) Repeated Phantom Force cycling by Dragapult burned 3 of our turns; we never used Kingambit's Sucker Punch pressure or a Protect-cycle to deny the emerging Phantom Force turn. 4) Rate-limit fallback on T2 meant one of ten turns was piloted blind.
[2026-10-02 19:14:56 EDT] [Team Inspiration] Recorded suggestion inspired by opponent build: "Copy their 'Phantom Force / U-turn evasive pivot' tempo idea by giving Mega Dragonite a bulk-leaning HP/SpD spread (survive one Inteleon Ice Beam at full HP after Multiscale) and testing Milotic with Icy Wind over Protect; Icy Wind both chips and denies the speed that Dragapult/Inteleon used to dictate every turn." (Reason: Dragapult cycled Phantom Force to dodge our damage and dictate timing while Inteleon's Ice Beam deleted both Whimsicott and Mega Dragonite in consecutive turns — a single Icy Wind would have flipped the speed order and let our bulkier pieces cash in damage before dying.)
