[2026-10-02 19:29:38 EDT]   [Review] What worked: Won in 6 turns vs SunnySleepy's sun team (Torkoal/Vileplume/Raichu-Y/Ditto). Turn-1 Weather Ball into Mega Raichu-Y was the correct win-condition denial: No Guard Zap Cannon would have OHKO'd Drogon and paralyzed the rest of the team, and sun-boosted Weather Ball OHKO'd it before it acted. Drogon's Drought flipping the field to sun also powered our Fire/Weather Ball damage. After Drogon died, the Milotic + Scarf Garchomp back half closed it cleanly: double-targeting Vileplume (the fast Chlorophyll special attacker) on T3 removed their real damage output, then Garchomp picked off Ditto over two turns while Milotic Recovered back into safety. Garchomp Choice Scarf again paid for itself (outspeeding transformed Ditto and Torkoal).
[2026-10-02 19:29:38 EDT]   [Review] What failed: Two avoidable losses of our own pieces. (1) T1: Whimsicott died immediately — Raichu-Y Fake Out flinch + Vileplume Acid Spray broke through the Sash in the same turn. The Sash only guarantees survival of ONE hit; a Fake Out user plus a second attacker is a two-hit turn, so the 'Sash makes Tailwind free' assumption is wrong when the opposing lead has Fake Out. Tailwind turns ended up 0. (2) T2: Drogon was KO'd by Ditto's Ancient Power. Ditto had just switched in on T1's faint — it transformed into one of our Pokemon (it copied Drogon's Charizard-Y data, giving it Ancient Power, 4x effective into our Drogon). Our listed 'Threats' line only showed Vileplume Sludge Wave 22-42% and completely ignored Ditto; we clicked Heat Wave instead of Protect/retreating the 4x-Rock-weak Mega against a fresh Ditto that mirrors our own team. That is a free Mega loss. (3) Minor: T2 Heat Wave was predicted to OHKO both and instead we lost the attacker before it resolved — the sequencing was never checked against Ditto's post-transform speed (Ditto copies stats and our Drogon is Speed 138, so a speed tie/loss was always possible).
[2026-10-02 19:29:38 EDT] [Team Inspiration] Recorded suggestion inspired by opponent build: "Copy their Fake Out + spread-damage opening (Raichu-Y Fake Out into Vileplume Acid Spray) by testing Milotic with Icy Wind over Protect so we own a non-priority speed-denial action; and consider that their Ditto proves our team is weak to its own mirror — a bulkier Mega Dragonite HP/SpD spread (survive one mirrored Draco/Ice attack at full HP via Multiscale) is a better Mega choice than Drogon versus any team carrying Ditto or Rock coverage." (Reason: They won both of our Pokemon losses this game with a two-action turn-1 burst (Fake Out breaks Sash, partner kills) and with a mirror Pokemon exploiting Drogon's 4x Rock weakness — we have no speed-drop tool and no safe Mega into Rock coverage.)
