[2026-10-02 19:48:29 EDT]   [Review] What worked: Turn 1 Milotic Protect correctly dodged the Rillaboom Wood Hammer/Grassy Glide OHKO threat, and the Mega Charizard-Y Drought immediately flipped Grassy Terrain's utility into our favor. Focus-firing Dragapult on T2 with Ice Beam + sun Weather Ball removed the fastest foe cleanly. Recognizing that Whimsicott at 1 HP should cash its action into Tailwind rather than Protect was the right application of the Focus Sash rule, and Tailwind did let Kingambit outspeed Flareon late. Kingambit's late Iron Head finally removed Flareon.
[2026-10-02 19:48:29 EDT]   [Review] What failed: 1) MISREAD THE FLASH FIRE SWITCH: on T1 they switched Flareon in on our Heat Wave, activating Flash Fire. From that moment Drogon's Fire STAB (Weather Ball in sun, Heat Wave) was dead weight against half their team, yet we kept Drogon in as the primary attacker for four more turns with only Ancient Power as real coverage. 2) DROGON DIED TO A FORESEEN ATTACK: Flareon Flare Blitz was listed in our own threat line as 43-72% from 'Last Resort' — we mis-scouted the moveset and left a 80% Drogon exposed to a Flash-Fire-boosted Flare Blitz that OHKO'd. We had Protect available. 3) TAILWIND DEFERRED TO TURN 5: three full turns of no speed control against a Scarf-feeling Flareon and a Primarina; by the time Tailwind landed, Whimsicott was at 1 HP and Drogon died the same turn, so we got exactly 3 Tailwind turns with only Kingambit and a 40% Milotic to use them. 4) WHIMSICOTT BURNT AS A PIVOT: switching Milotic→Whimsicott into a Flare Blitz turn put our Sash setter at 1 HP before it ever acted — the exact 'Whimsicott survival rule' we wrote. The correct pivot was Kingambit (resists nothing of Fire but is far bulkier and immune to the Grass priority in Grassy Terrain). 5) T6-T7 OVERKILL/WHIFF: we spent two turns aiming Kowtow Cleave at a 14-31% Flareon that Detected once and then switched out, while Rillaboom freely re-set Grassy Terrain; no action was ever directed at Rillaboom, which then killed Milotic and Kingambit.
