[2026-10-02 19:51:04 EDT]   [Review] What worked: Vs popandpop (WIN, 4 turns): the Kingambit + Drogon lead into a Trick Room/Armor Tail team was correct. Turn 1 Protect on Drogon against a Glimmora holding an unused Mega Stone (Power Gem is 4x on Charizard-Y) was textbook win-con preservation, and Kingambit's Iron Head — chosen over Sucker Punch because Farigiraf's Armor Tail blocks priority — put Glimmora to 27% before Toxic Debris/Spiky Shield healed it. Turn 2 Weather Ball in sun OHKO'd Farigiraf, simultaneously removing the Trick Room setter AND the Armor Tail priority blocker, which is the exact 'kill the engine, not the attacker' directive. Turn 3 Iron Head punched through Clefable's Follow Me for the KO and Weather Ball chipped it to 4% first — focus fire on the redirector worked. Opponent forfeited at 2-0 down with us having lost nothing.
[2026-10-02 19:51:04 EDT]   [Review] What failed: Minor: Turn 2 Kingambit's Iron Head hit Glimmora's Spiky Shield — a wasted action plus 25 HP contact recoil. Glimmora at 52% after Toxic-Debris healing had already shown it was the Protect-prone slot, and the Wolfe rule 'the more obvious their Protect is, the more likely they Protect that slot' applied: the correct line was Iron Head into Farigiraf (or Clefable's eventual slot) while Weather Ball handled the other, converting their Protect into a free turn for us instead of for them. Turn 4 double-committed Drogon to Protect again while Kingambit attacked a 52% Glimmora that had Spiky Shielded once already — a second likely-wasted action, saved only by the forfeit. Also, Farigiraf's Trick on turn 1 swapped an item onto Kingambit (likely Choice-locking it); the pilot never accounted for the possible Choice lock in subsequent turns, which was pure luck that Iron Head stayed the right move. Finally, Tailwind was never relevant (Whimsicott/Garchomp unused), fine in a 4-turn win but note 0 Tailwind turns again.
[2026-10-02 19:51:04 EDT] [Team Inspiration] Recorded suggestion inspired by opponent build: "They ran a hazard/chip + redirection + Armor Tail shell (Glimmora Toxic Debris/Spiky Shield, Farigiraf Trick + Armor Tail, Clefable Follow Me). Mirror the redirection half: test Whimsicott with Helping Hand or keep Encore, but more importantly give Milotic Icy Wind over Protect so we own a non-Prankster speed-control action that still works when Whimsicott is dead or blocked — and consider Clear Amulet on Kingambit so Trick/Intimidate/stat shenanigans cannot cripple our lead piece." (Reason: Farigiraf's turn-1 Trick onto Kingambit could have Choice-locked our main lead into a bad move for the whole game; a Clear Amulet does not stop Trick but an item we care about losing does matter, and their redirection/disruption engine (Follow Me + Spiky Shield) bought them free turns that only a second speed-control source or an Encore would have punished.)
