[2026-10-02 20:13:20 EDT]   [Review] What failed: 1) Turn-1 Tailwind was blanked by Sneasler Fake Out: Whimsicott lost its action and its Sash buffer, then died to Overheat on turn 2 — our only speed source gone by turn 2 for the 133rd time in 213 games. Leading a Fake-Out-vulnerable Prankster setter opposite a previewed Fake Out user is the known failure pattern. 2) Severe damage-calc miscalibration again: Weather Ball on Sneasler was predicted 13-25% and dealt 100%. A 4x-underestimated calc means our move selection is running on bad numbers; if the engine had believed the real number it would never have considered an alternative. 3) Turn 2 we left Whimsicott exposed with no Protect while it was the slot with the lower listed threat but the actual fatal one (Rotom Overheat was not in the threat list at all because Rotom had switched out and back). Threat lists built only from currently-active foes under-report switch-back attackers.
