[2026-10-02 21:16:18 EDT]   [Review] What worked: Leading Kingambit into Farigiraf Trick Room was correct and paid off instantly: Kowtow Cleave + Garchomp chip KO'd the Trick Room setter on turn 1 before it ever moved, so Trick Room never came up all game. Kingambit also traded itself for Sylveon (Iron Head OHKO) and Defiant turned Staraptor's Intimidate into +2. Dragonite + Garchomp cleaned up Torkoal, removing sun/Eruption. We won the speed-control war on paper (6 Tailwind turns to 0).
[2026-10-02 21:16:18 EDT]   [Review] What failed: 1) Garchomp spent at least four full actions clicking Stomping Tantrum into a Flying-type Staraptor (0 damage, repeated immunity messages). That is half our action economy donated for multiple turns and is exactly the 'Choice-locked into a useless move -> switch out' rule we already have written down. 2) We never punished Mega Staraptor's Close Combat Defense/SpD... actually it boosted def/spd (Contrary-like via Close Combat? No — it boosted, meaning Contrary Staraptor), and we kept trading into it instead of focusing it down or switching to Milotic, which we never even brought. 3) We burned turns 5-6 chipping a 44% Torkoal through two Protects while Staraptor Mega-evolved for free and started snowballing. 4) The endgame was a 20-turn grind where a +Def/+SpD Contrary Mega Staraptor had both speed (after our Tailwind lapsed) and power — exactly the board state we are told never to allow. 5) Whimsicott contributed only 47% damage and never got a second Tailwind out before dying.
