[2026-10-02 22:37:23 EDT]   [Review] What worked: Win vs unsupervised702 (Trick Room archetype, Kingambit + Mega Dragonite lead). Turn 1 focus-fire on Sneasler with Iron Head + Dragon Pulse was the correct Wolfe play: Sneasler Close Combat OHKOs Kingambit, so removing it before it could act was win-condition denial. Turn 3 Heat Wave scored a clean double KO on burned Rillaboom and Protect-healed Sneasler — the turn-2 Heat Wave burn on Rillaboom is what converted that into a 2-for-1. Turn 4 Kowtow Cleave deleted Farigiraf, removing both Armor Tail (priority block) and the Trick Room setter in one action. Endgame 2v1 was closed with the safe double-target (Moonblast + Ice Beam) rather than a prediction, exactly per the 'ahead in count = no reads' directive.
[2026-10-02 22:37:23 EDT]   [Review] What failed: 1) Lead choice: Kingambit into Rillaboom (Fake Out + High Horsepower) lost turn 1's Kingambit action to flinch and lost 60% of its HP to Ground chip. 2) Turn 2 double-attack into an obvious Protect: Sneasler at 28% HP was the single most predictable Protect on the board, and we aimed BOTH Iron Head and Heat Wave at it; Iron Head was fully wasted and Heat Wave only landed on Rillaboom by spread splash. The correct line was Iron Head/attack the Rillaboom slot and let Heat Wave's spread chip Sneasler. 3) Turn 4 we let Mega Salamence enter and Hyper Voice for a double KO (Dragonite + Kingambit in one move) — we had no Protect on the 60/168 Dragonite despite Draco Meteor/Hyper Voice being displayed as a KO threat. That nearly threw a won game; Milotic cleaned up only because Whimsicott's Moonblast rolled high. 4) Damage calc was off twice on Dragonite's hits (Dragon Pulse 78% vs predicted 61% max, Heat Wave 62% vs 56% max), suggesting our calc under-rates sun-boosted/Mega Dragonite output — we are leaving KOs on the table by assuming we can't kill.
