[2026-10-02 22:46:35 EDT]   [Review] What worked: Won 4-0 in Pokémon remaining... actually a clean win vs LLCDoubleOG's Trick Room/offense shell. The Whimsicott + Drogon lead was correct: turn-1 Protect on Whimsicott dodged a lethal Dire Claw/Make It Rain and let Drogon Mega-evolve and set Sun. Kingambit's Kowtow Cleave one-shot Gholdengo (Dark hits Ghost/Steel for the KO, and Kingambit is immune to nothing relevant but tanks Make It Rain for only 21-33%). Tailwind on turn 2 was correctly set BEFORE any Trick Room appeared and gave us the speed lead for the rest of the game. The closing turn was textbook: Dragonite's sun-boosted Heat Wave hit both sub-10% foes for a double KO while Kingambit Protected through Volcarona Heat Wave — Rage Powder could not redirect the spread move, so the game ended with zero risk.
[2026-10-02 22:46:35 EDT]   [Review] What failed: Drogon again contributed 98% damage and zero KOs before dying on turn 2 — the fifth straight game where our Mega Charizard is removed early. Specific chain: T1 Sneasler Fake Out (flinch + Dire Claw poison) plus Gholdengo Shadow Ball put Drogon at 20% before it ever moved; T2 Gholdengo Protected our Heat Wave so the spread only hit Sneasler, and Dire Claw finished Drogon. The Gholdengo Protect was predictable — it was the obvious KO target after a 53-85% Heat Wave the prior turn, and we fired a spread move into it anyway rather than accounting for the 50% damage loss. T4 we chose Moonblast into Volcarona (non-lethal chip) while Sneasler at 2% was free to Fake Out — Whimsicott got flinched and then died to Volcarona Heat Wave. Had we Moonblasted the 2% Sneasler (it was the active slot p1b) we would have removed the Fake Out and kept Whimsicott. The damage model was again optimistic-low: Kowtow Cleave predicted 52-61% on Volcarona and dealt 77%.
[2026-10-02 22:46:35 EDT] [Team Inspiration] Recorded suggestion inspired by opponent build: "Give Drogon a Covert Cloak in place of its current item slot consideration is impossible (Charizardite Y is mandatory) — instead swap Mega Dragonite's Heat Wave for Extreme Speed and bring Dragonite as the primary Mega against any sheet with two Fake Out users. Alternatively, lead Kingambit (Fake Out-resistant bulk, Defiant) alongside Whimsicott and bring Drogon in on turn 3 after the Fake Out is spent." (Reason: Their whole opening was Sneasler Fake Out + Gholdengo Shadow Ball to delete our Mega before it acted — the same pattern that has killed Drogon in five straight games. We cannot run Covert Cloak on a Mega Stone holder, so the fix is either a priority finisher on Dragonite or delaying Drogon's entry past the Fake Out turn.)
