[2026-10-02 23:14:08 EDT]   [Review] What worked: Whimsicott + Mega Charizard-Y lead removed their Whimsicott (speed control setter) on turn 1 with Heat Wave, denying them any Tailwind refresh. Turn 2 Protect on Drogon vs Arcanine-Hisui Head Smash (235-384% OHKO displayed) was textbook — the Protect-Drogon rule saved our Mega and it later closed the game. Turn 3 was a clean Macro Safe Play: sacrificing a 1-HP Whimsicott while pivoting Drogon out to Milotic, who ate Intimidate for +2 SpA (Competitive) and then OHKO'd Mega Salamence with Ice Beam. Milotic Protect cycling vs a Protect-spamming Arcanine stalled perfectly and Recover/Leftovers kept it alive. Kingambit converted at 1 HP with Kowtow Cleave on Dragapult.
[2026-10-02 23:14:08 EDT]   [Review] What failed: 1) Turn 6 Milotic Scald into Arcanine, which had Protected the previous turn — a fully predictable wasted action; aiming Scald at Dragapult (or Protecting Milotic) was free. That wasted action cost Milotic ~90% HP from Phantom Force and nearly lost a won game. 2) Turn 5 Kowtow Cleave missed (85% accuracy) into Dragapult while we were ahead — Wolfe's anti-variance rule says prefer the 100%-accurate line when ahead, though here Kowtow was the only KO. 3) Turn 1 Moonblast missed; nothing to fix. 4) Kingambit was allowed to stay in at 21 HP into Arcanine Flare Blitz range on turn 6 instead of Protecting — Life Orb recoil then finished it; we traded our Kingambit for a KO we would have gotten anyway.
