[2026-10-02 23:49:49 EDT]   [Review] What worked: Kingambit + Mega Charizard-Y lead into Psychic Terrain (psyterrain / Charizard|zk) delivered a clean 4-0 win over Gellapo in 5 turns. Kingambit was immune to Expanding Force and Kowtow Cleave ignored Milotic's Protect-timing by pressuring every turn; Drogon's Drought turned Weather Ball into a 150 BP nuke that OHKO'd Indeedee, Hydrapple and Mega-bulk Golisopod. Turn 4's declared double-KO (Kowtow on Milotic at 42% + Weather Ball on Hydrapple at 33%) was textbook 2-action economy: two actions, two KOs, no overlap. Turn 5 Protect on a 25% HP Kingambit while Drogon took the guaranteed last KO was correct safe-play-when-ahead discipline.
[2026-10-02 23:49:49 EDT]   [Review] What failed: Only one real error, but a recurring one: T3 both of our actions were spent as if Milotic could not Protect. Milotic at 30% HP with Recover already revealed is the single most predictable Protect on the board; Kowtow Cleave hit the shield and we traded a full action for zero damage while Hydrapple removed 59% of Kingambit. The correct T3 line was Kingambit Protect (dodging Earth Power, it is 4x-relevant special pressure on a Life-Orb-chipped body) or Kingambit attacking Hydrapple alongside Weather Ball to delete the Ground attacker outright. We also never used Whimsicott/Milotic — fine given the speed of the win, but it means no Tailwind data. Macro-wise nothing was lost; the game was won on turn 4.
[2026-10-02 23:49:49 EDT] [Team Inspiration] Recorded suggestion inspired by opponent build: "Gellapo's bulky Milotic (Recover + Protect) stalled two of our actions on 202 HP; mirror that durability tax by keeping Recover-Protect Milotic but shifting Mega Dragonite's Heat Wave (fully redundant with Charizard-Y sun Heat Wave) to Extreme Speed, giving us a +2 priority finisher that closes Protect-cycling bulky walls and 1-HP Sash setters the turn they drop." (Reason: Our only wasted action this game was a single-target KO attempt into a predictable Protect; priority damage ignores the Protect-timing game entirely and is the one tool this team still lacks (confirmed across the grynpup, Suttirak, Lawliet0 and appledragon3 reviews).)
