[2026-10-02 23:57:01 EDT]   [Review] What worked: Won 4-1 in Pokémon count vs gogogadgetnuke's Alolan-Ninetales snow team. Turn 1 Prankster Tailwind landed before Ninetales acted, giving us 3 speed-control turns. Recognizing the Encore lock on Whimsicott and immediately switching it to Kingambit (T2) was the correct 'switch when Encored into a useless move' play from the standing rules. Kingambit Iron Head/Kowtow Cleave removed Rillaboom through Grassy Terrain recovery, and Milotic was the MVP: +2 SpA from Incineroar's Intimidate (Competitive) turned Ice Beam into a clean OHKO on Mega Dragonite and Scald into an OHKO on Incineroar. Milotic Protect on T4 blanked Rillaboom's Fake Out while Kingambit got the free Kowtow KO — a textbook 'Attack Slot A + Protect Slot B' turn. Endgame Moonblast finishing at 1 HP Whimsicott was correct use of the 1-HP action rule.
[2026-10-02 23:57:01 EDT]   [Review] What failed: 1) PLAN ERROR: brought Mega Dragonite vs an Alolan-Ninetales snow team. The standing snow rule says Charizard-Y is mandatory (Drought overwrites Snowscape, removing Blizzard's 100% accuracy and the Aurora Veil tempo). We lost our Mega for free on turn 2. 2) T1 Heat Wave spread chipped their Dragonite by 7% but, critically, revealed/committed our Mega into a mirror matchup where their Mega Dragonite outspeeds post-Tailwind and Draco Meteor OHKOs a Multiscale-broken Dragonite. The correct T1 was Tailwind + Protect (or Heat Wave aimed with Dragonite behind Protect) because Ninetales Blizzard showed a 79-136% OHKO roll on Dragonite — our own threat display literally printed 'OHKO 63%' and we attacked anyway. That is the HARD OHKO-BAND violation again. 3) T2 we stayed in with Dragonite at 168 HP into a board where Blizzard + Draco Meteor was lethal; the switch should have been Dragonite out, not Whimsicott out (Whimsicott Encored into Tailwind was harmless; it could have sat there). 4) T3 Milotic Ice Beam was fired into an obvious Protect from a Dragonite that had just taken a Mega-vs-Mega trade and was the only foe we threatened — exactly the PREDICTABLE-PROTECT pattern on our proposal list. 5) We burned 2 of 8 Claude calls on rate-limit fallbacks, including team preview, which is how the wrong Mega got brought at all.
