[2026-10-03 00:06:35 EDT]   [Review] What worked: Kingambit lead vs Farigiraf Trick Room was correct in principle; Mega Charizard-Y Heat Wave on T2 was the game-winning turn, double-KOing Farigiraf (the TR setter) and Tsareena (the Low Kick/Triple Axel threat) in one action — a perfect 2-for-1 under Trick Room. Milotic Protect on T2 and T3 correctly dodged Triple Axel/Eruption while the sun Heat Wave landed. The endgame 1v1 Milotic vs Clawitzer was played exactly right: Scald for the burn, then Recover-cycle attrition, converting a 1-mon deficit position into a win.
[2026-10-03 00:06:35 EDT]   [Review] What failed: 1) T1 fallback (rate limit) chose Milotic Scald + Kingambit Kowtow into Farigiraf, ignoring that Tsareena's Low Kick OHKOs our 207-HP Kingambit; we lost our anti-TR piece on turn 1 for 30% chip. 2) T4: Drogon at 41% attacked instead of Protecting/switching into Torkoal's Weather Ball (sun-boosted Fire, 100 BP) under Trick Room — Torkoal moves first, so Drogon was dead before it could fire. The displayed threat only listed Clawitzer Dragon Pulse and omitted Torkoal Weather Ball entirely, even though Weather Ball had just been used. 3) T5: Garchomp was sent in and immediately died to Clawitzer Ice Beam (4x) — a known 4x matchup; Milotic should have been the lone body with Garchomp held back or we should have accepted the 1v2. We won anyway only because Milotic out-stalled Clawitzer. 4) Three rate-limit fallbacks/preview misses continue to cost whole turns.
